{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">2023 AMC 10A #3</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2023 AMC 12A #3</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(slightly_refined)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (slightly refined)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Pablo&#39;s_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Pablo's Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive perfect squares less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc4d43132a9440c99ab434591f08bd72c3adacc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }9 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }10 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }11 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28slightly_refined.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(slightly_refined)\">Solution 1 (slightly refined)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (slightly refined)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5833ccfa1d765436f830bb012a4a4edba8bd1877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor{\\sqrt{2023}}\\right \\rfloor = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"34\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50139fbd7aa05d9c36918932366275feb9bd13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor{\\frac{44}{5}}\\right \\rfloor = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) 8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"125\" height=\"45\" /> perfect squares less than 2023 that are divisible by 5.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is square-free, each solution must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab660081d421ba9ad93273259efac9a7e27639a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />. We take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dced76b1e07adcc5024973539550cf19bc7769f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor{\\frac{2023}{25}}\\right \\rfloor = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"105\" height=\"45\" /> and see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b4f4712a75c61ee695f7cd10c58f6b60126e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) 8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" /> positive perfect squares no greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~jwseph\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the perfect squares have to be divisible by 5, then we know it has to be 5 times some number squared <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edffdc54db56482ae3e2990d7bd0623c68dc143f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5 \\cdot x)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"21\" />. With this information, you can figure out every single product of 5 and another number squared to count how many perfect squares are divisible by 5 that are less than 2023. (EX: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463d929517201f98abc4b71ad365036b927a0b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^{2} = 25, 10^{2} = 100, ... 40^{2} = 1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />) With this you get a max of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/0/10036d5ecec4e8d14a2454aee2f4c8098dba8248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />, or  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50139fbd7aa05d9c36918932366275feb9bd13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor{\\frac{44}{5}}\\right \\rfloor = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) 8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"125\" height=\"45\" /> solutions. \n</p><p>~BlueShardow                                                                                                                                 \n~NOOK(Minor LaTeX edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The way of BlueShardow refined:\n</p><p>All it takes is to recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squared is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c592fe37e2d028ad1e4e0a1a9d178e2f31d51b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. So all the squares of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90503655bb7fa6620fde8e2bd2aa75fdd142307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 1, 5 \\cdot 2, 5 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" /> so on are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. It can be done even if one does not remember that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squared is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78db23e86da8fe319c63bdb5eaf6d3fd8fefa17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, all it takes is intuition. One can easily see mentally that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc5fbd1ea2c22b763a9f8a5b30028ac7d7cde78b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squared is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc314f9ecb9c2b3c96a327f5191f1d5b13d8e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />, and then one has to do just one more computation and see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c592fe37e2d028ad1e4e0a1a9d178e2f31d51b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squared exceeds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>~edit by RobinDaBank\n</p><p>Note that you can find the square of any number that ends in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by taking the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than it and the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than it, multiplying those together, and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. For example, to calculate the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27da4fca6f3fecb215974023aad210b70ec3857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, you do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d573a511bff4834c58f69da1d42f749d4309de6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40 \\cdot 50 = 2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f613966cda2e46e930104eefd561e24032aafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000 + 25 = 2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>And then you know that it goes up from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the multiples of five are {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />..., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />}, dividing each of them by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, you get {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />..., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />}, therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b4f4712a75c61ee695f7cd10c58f6b60126e7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) 8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"58\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~note by amadeus1011, edited by mihikamishra, then edited by ~NXC (minor latex edits by mw2014)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Little Fermat\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=3FSk6sTPCUg9J0U1&amp;t=394\">https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=3FSk6sTPCUg9J0U1&amp;t=394</a>\n~little-fermat\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X\">Video Solution by Math-X</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=rwUloGNfN7tcoG-8&amp;t=502\">https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=rwUloGNfN7tcoG-8&amp;t=502</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=aIYHWEU82uUu21fQ&amp;t=165\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=aIYHWEU82uUu21fQ&amp;t=165</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod\">Video Solution by CosineMethod</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wNH6O8D-7dY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wNH6O8D-7dY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/w7RBPIatRNE\">https://youtu.be/w7RBPIatRNE</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Z3fmCkuHG3c\">https://youtu.be/Z3fmCkuHG3c</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power